Ideas, re-written in our own code, from NeonClipping (https://github.com/iamajmeena/neonclipping,
MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Ajay K Meena and NeonClipping contributors; studied at commit 0525004):
  - clipstudio/ytcaptions.py: YouTube's own word-timed json3 captions as the transcript;
  - clipstudio/livechat.py: reading Twitch chat anonymously during a live stream, the 10 s bucket /
    5-minute baseline spike rule and a hype meter;
  - clipstudio/encoders.py: trying hardware encoders and falling back to x264;
  - clipstudio/signals.py: raised-voice (2-4 kHz), police-light flicker and flash cues (measured on
    the test set; not used by the picker because they did not help).
The MIT License text above applies to those ideas as it does to the plugin's patterns.

No code from the Clips Kitty application itself (ColinGPT9/clips-studio, AGPL-3.0) is used; only
its public README was read.
